<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashikaga Yoshiteru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1536">1536</a>–<a href="/years/1565">1565</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashikaga Yoshiteru was the thirteenth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> of the Ashikaga shogunate, holding the office from 1546 to 1565. For much of his rule he was overshadowed or driven from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miyoshi-nagayoshi">Miyoshi Nagayoshi</a>, while trying to restore shogunal authority by mediating between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> and studying swordsmanship. In 1565 forces of the Miyoshi elders and Matsunaga Hisamichi attacked his residence and killed him, an event known as the Eiroku Incident.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshiteru.jpg" alt="Ashikaga Yoshiteru" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Tosa Mitsuyoshi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashikaga_Yoshiteru_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
